how do i get a deepseek spi key
Read 10 web pages
Getting your DeepSeek API key is straightforward. Here's the step-by-step process, working class hero style 👇

🎯 Quick Steps to Get Your DeepSeek API Key
Step 1: Go to DeepSeek Platform
Head to: https://platform.deepseek.com 

Step 2: Sign Up / Log In
Click "Sign Up" in the top right

Use your email or phone number to register 

Verify your email (code arrives in ~1 minute)

Set a strong password

Step 3: Navigate to API Keys
Once logged in:

Look at the left sidebar

Click "API Keys" 

Step 4: Create Your Key
Click "Create new API Key" or "Create" button 

Give it a name (e.g., my-pdf-research-agent or vibe-coding-project)

Click "Create" 

Step 5: COPY YOUR KEY IMMEDIATELY ⚠️
A popup will show your API key

CLICK COPY right away

Paste it somewhere safe (like a password manager or a secure notes app)

🚨 CRITICAL: The key only shows ONCE. If you close the window without copying it, you'll have to delete that key and create a new one. 

Step 6: Add Credits (if needed)
DeepSeek sometimes gives free credits to new users (check your dashboard) 

If you don't have credits, you'll need to add payment method and top up

Good news: DeepSeek is CHEAP (~$0.14 per million tokens, so a few dollars will last a long time) 

💰 Pricing Reality Check
~$0.14 per 1 million tokens (input)

~$0.28 per 1 million tokens (output)

Your PDF research analysis will cost pennies — like $0.01-0.05 per run 

🔒 Keep It Safe (Seriously)
NEVER put your API key directly in your code

NEVER upload it to GitHub

ALWAYS use environment variables (like we set up with $env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY) 

🚀 Set It Up For Your Project
After you have your key, open your terminal (where you run Streamlit) and set it:

Windows PowerShell:

powershell
$env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-your-actual-key-here"
Windows Command Prompt:

cmd
set DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-actual-key-here
Mac/Linux:

bash
export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-your-actual-key-here"
Then run your app:

bash
streamlit run app.py
❓ No Free Credits?
If you sign up and see zero balance:

Go to "Billing" in the left sidebar

Add minimum top-up ($5-10 will last you months for this project)

DeepSeek is one of the cheapest LLM APIs out there 

